+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-launch review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Two of the findings below are ship-blockers on their own:
+
+1. **`deposit()` reverts against the real USDT at `0xdAC17F95…`.** Not "might fail
+   under some conditions" — every deposit, always. Proven on a mainnet fork against
+   the real token and the real Aave pool. The vault is dead on arrival.
+2. **The yield vault pays no yield.** `totalAssets()` returns a stored integer that
+   is never reconciled against the aUSDT position. Every dollar of Aave interest is
+   permanently stranded in the vault with no code path that can ever release it.
+   Depositors withdraw *less* than they put in, forever.
+
+The 39 passing tests are not wrong; they are testing a different contract than the
+one you are deploying. `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a standard OpenZeppelin ERC20,
+and `test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` mints an aToken whose balance never changes. Those
+two mocks define away exactly the two behaviours that break the vault: USDT's
+non-standard ABI, and aToken rebasing. 100% line coverage measures which lines ran,
+not whether the assumptions behind them hold.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+Nothing under `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` or `test/mocks/` was modified. All
+new material is in new files:
+
+| File | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test/fork/MainnetUsdt.t.sol` | Fork tests against real USDT / real Aave V3 pool |
+| `test/audit/AuditMocks.sol` | A USDT-faithful token, a fee-charging token, an interest-accruing Aave pool |
+| `test/audit/Accounting.t.sol` | Ten failing tests, one per finding |
+| `test/audit/Invariants.t.sol` | Stateful invariant campaign |
+| `test/audit/NegativeResults.t.sol` | Attacks I tried that do **not** work (these pass) |
+
+The fork tests need an **archive** RPC (they pin block 26,000,000). They default to
+`https://eth.drpc.org`, which served every request in this review; override with
+`MAINNET_RPC_URL=<your endpoint>` if you prefer. Pruned endpoints such as
+`1rpc.io/eth` or `publicnode` will fail with "state at block … is pruned" / 403,
+which is an RPC limitation, not a test failure.
+
+### The baseline, confirmed first
